Also, bless the arrows and get as lucky as you can, so they don't
dissapear as often.

A fun thing to do once you get the longbow, is to walk around for a
while without shooting anything and invoke it as often as possible (I
was doing every 100 turns,but I don't know if that's optimal). My one
ascention was a ranger. I built up a stock of over 700 arrows using
the longbow and arrow traps, then enchanted them. The arrows didn't
dissapear often, but you need to shoot about 200 of them to clear a
nice-sized zoo or graveyard if you don't pick them back up right away.

Of course you could just get an artifact melee weapon instead, which
is aparently more common.

Two more things, increase damage rings work per-arrow (so the effect
is multiplied), so if you find one, charge it, name it precious and
keep it on. The other is that you can shoot one extra elven arrow from
your bow (3 on average), so, if possible, enchant and save your elven
arrows for especial occasions.

